{"type":"message","id":"197f882e","parentId":"a9e62c80","timestamp":"2026-05-18T13:00:39.761Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_Mdwi35JgCcO5QSTJsFjZYvRj","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# COINOGRAPHY EDITORIAL TEMPLATE\n\nThis document is your absolute source of truth. You MUST write the article EXACTLY following the numbered sections below. Deviation is strictly prohibited.\n\n## 🔴 CRITICAL WRITING RULES (READ FIRST)\n- **NO EM-DASHES:** Never use the `—` character anywhere in the article. Replace with a comma, a period, or restructure the sentence.\n- **NATURAL WRITING:** Never use AI phrases: \"it's worth noting\", \"it is important to note\", \"delve into\", \"in conclusion\", \"furthermore\", \"moreover\", \"in summary\", \"the crypto landscape\", \"the world of crypto\", \"a testament to\", \"shed light on\".\n- **TONE:** Direct. Trader-focused. Analytical. No hype, no fluff, no adjectives like \"amazing\" or \"shocking.\"\n- **PARAGRAPHS:** 1–4 sentences max. Break aggressively. One idea per paragraph.\n- **BULLET LISTS:** 3–4 items only. Used inside H3 sections only. Never in the conclusion or opening.\n- **ANCHOR LINKS:** You MUST naturally embed 2-3 markdown links inside the body text. These links MUST point to the exact source URLs provided in your RESEARCH_JSON. Example: `[according to recent data from Decrypt](https://decrypt.co/...)`\n- **CHART SOURCES:** The orchestrator will provide the charts. Simply embed exactly 2 mentions of the `[CHART_PLACEHOLDER]` tag inside the H2 sections.\n- **KEYWORD PLACEMENT:** \n  - Primary keyword in H1 (first 5 words)\n  - Primary keyword in first 100 words (opening hook)\n  - Primary keyword in at least one H2 and the Conclusion\n  - Secondary keywords must appear in H2 headings and their body paragraphs.\n\n## 🛠️ PRE-FLIGHT CHECKLIST\nBefore generating any text, in your `<thinking>` block, confirm:\n- [ ] I have the primary and secondary keywords.\n- [ ] I have the source URLs from the `RESEARCH_JSON` input.\n- [ ] I will write EXACTLY in this order: META → Hook → H2#1 → H2#2 → Conclusion → FAQs → Sources.\n- [ ] I will write NOTHING outside this order.\n\n============================\nARTICLE STRUCTURE (STRICT)\n============================\n\n### SECTION 1 (REQUIRED): META BLOCK\nOutput this exact block at the very top. No conversational filler before it. The very first word must be \"META\".\n- SEO Title: [50–60 characters maximum — MUST follow formula: Primary Keyword + Brand Name + Value]\n- Meta Description: [150–160 characters maximum — MUST follow formula: What the article offers + Unique angle + Call to Action]\n- URL Slug: [lowercase-hyphens-only, e.g. bitcoin-price-hits-new-all-time-high]\n- Categories: [e.g. Bitcoin News, Latest News]\n- Primary Keyword: [e.g. \"Bitcoin price drop\"]\n- Secondary Keywords: [e.g. \"BTC resistance\", \"crypto market pullback\", \"$80K Bitcoin\"]\n\n---\n\n### SECTION 2 (REQUIRED): OPENING HOOK\n**# [H1 Title — must contain primary keyword in first 5 words, include a price or number]**\n\n*(Do NOT add an H2 heading above these paragraphs)*\nPara 1: State the core event with a specific price or data point. 2–3 sentences. Start with the primary keyword naturally. Be direct.\nPara 2: Market reaction or supporting data. One additional observation (volume, altcoins, funding rates). 2–3 sentences.\nPara 3: One-line reframe that sets the article's tone. (\"This isn't panic. It looks like traders taking money off the table after a strong run.\")\n\n---\n\n### SECTION 3 (REQUIRED): FIRST H2 SECTION\n**## [Secondary Keyword 1]: [What It Means / Signals / Shows]**\n\n[1–2 intro paragraphs explaining the news at a high level.]\n[CHART_PLACEHOLDER]\n\n**### [Sub-angle 1: e.g. \"Profit-Taking Shows Up at Resistance\"]**\n[1–2 short paragraphs]\n[Optional 3-item bullet list]\n\n**### [Sub-angle 2: e.g. \"Altcoins Start Losing Steam\"]**\n[2–3 very short paragraphs — 1 to 3 sentences each]\n\n---\n\n### SECTION 4 (REQUIRED): SECOND H2 SECTION\n**## Key [Levels / Data Signals / Numbers] Traders Should Watch [Now / Next]**\n\n[1 intro paragraph]\n[CHART_PLACEHOLDER]\n\n**### [Level/Signal 1: e.g. \"$75K Needs to Hold\"]**\n[1 paragraph — what this level means, what happens if it holds/breaks]\n\n**### [Level/Signal 2: e.g. \"$80K Remains the Barrier\"]**\n[1 paragraph]\n[Required 3-item bullet list starting with \"Look for:\"]\n\n---\n\n### SECTION 5 (REQUIRED): CONCLUSION\n**## Conclusion**\n\nPara 1: Restate the core event in one sentence using the primary keyword. Name the key level or data point.\nPara 2: What it means for the near-term structure. One or two clean sentences.\nPara 3: Actionable close for the reader. What they should do or watch. End on a direct, confident note.\n\n---\n\n### SECTION 6 (REQUIRED): FAQS\n**## FAQs**\n\n**1. Why did [primary event] happen?**\n[3–4 sentence answer. Target ~60 words.]\n\n**2. Is this the start of a bigger [correction/rally/trend]?**\n[3–4 sentence answer. Target ~60 words.]\n\n**3. What [levels/signals] should traders watch now?**\n[3–4 sentence answer. Target ~60 words.]\n\n**4. How does this affect [related asset/market sector]?**\n[3–4 sentence answer. Target ~60 words.]\n\n**5. What is the historical context for this move?**\n[3–4 sentence answer. Target ~60 words.]\n\n**6. What are the short-term risks for investors?**\n[3–4 sentence answer. Target ~60 words.]\n\n---\n\n### SECTION 7 (REQUIRED): SOURCES FOOTER\n**Sources:**\n- [Publication Name]: [source URL from research facts]\n- [Publication Name]: [source URL from research facts]\n\nSTOP GENERATING HERE. DO NOT ADD ANY BROADER CONTEXT SECTIONS. \nState your final word count on the last line of your output as: [Word Count: XXXX]\n\n## 🛡️ POST-OUTPUT VERIFICATION\nBefore finalizing your generation, mentally verify:\n[ ] Exactly 1 H1, 2 H2s, 4 H3s, Conclusion, FAQs, Sources?\n[ ] No em-dashes anywhere?\n[ ] Primary keyword in H1 first 5 words?\n[ ] 2-3 anchor links embedded in body text pointing to source URLs?\n[ ] Word count stated on final line?\n[ ] No sections added beyond the 7 defined above?\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1779109239760}}
{"type":"message","id":"b0a1d59d","parentId":"197f882e","timestamp":"2026-05-18T13:01:45.576Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_xypHFh4MIdDsuUOPX3jjF2SV","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\ntext = '''META\nSEO Title: Bitcoin selloff | Coinography levels and liquidation risk\nMeta Description: See why Bitcoin dropped below $77K, how Iran tension and $677M in liquidations hit risk assets, and which BTC levels traders should watch next.\nURL Slug: bitcoin-selloff-below-77k-trump-iran-warning\nCategories: Bitcoin News, Latest News\nPrimary Keyword: Bitcoin selloff\nSecondary Keywords: crypto market pullback, BTC support levels, Bitcoin liquidations\n\n# Bitcoin selloff sends BTC to $76K after Iran warning\n\nBitcoin selloff pressure pushed BTC to about $76,500 in early Asian trading on Monday, wiping out the rebound that had carried the market higher since May 1. The drop put the asset back at a three-week low after traders reacted to Donald Trump's warning that the \"clock is ticking\" for Iran.\n\nDerivatives desks felt the move fast. [According to CoinTelegraph](https://cointelegraph.com/markets/bitcoin-falls-to-76k-after-trump-says-clock-is-ticking-for-iran?utm_source=rss_feed&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound), more than $607 million in long positions were liquidated across crypto in 24 hours, while total forced liquidations neared $677 million as oil jumped and broader risk appetite cracked. Ether, Solana, and XRP also turned lower, showing this was not an isolated BTC flush.\n\nThis is not blind panic. It looks like a macro-driven reset after a crowded upside trade.\n\n## Crypto market pullback: What It Shows\n\nThis crypto market pullback started with headlines outside crypto, but it quickly became a positioning story. Bitcoin had been trading near 13-week highs close to $83,000, so the market was vulnerable once a geopolitical shock hit.\n\nCoinDesk framed the move as Bitcoin slipping below $77,000 after Trump's Iran warning rattled risk assets, tying the drop to higher oil and weaker sentiment [in its market coverage](https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/05/18/bitcoin-slides-below-usd77-000-as-trump-s-iran-warning-rattles-risk-assets). That matters because the selloff was not driven by a broken onchain narrative or a sudden crypto-specific failure. It was a fast repricing of risk across markets.\n\n[CHART_PLACEHOLDER]\n\n### Liquidations Show the Long Trade Was Crowded\n\nThe cleanest signal inside this drop is the size of the derivatives unwind. When a market falls on negative headlines and forced selling accelerates, price can overshoot because liquidated longs have to close immediately.\n\nThat is what Bitcoin liquidations looked like on Monday. Traders who chased the recent breakout lost control of the tape, and spot buyers were not aggressive enough to absorb the wave on first contact.\n\n- Long liquidations rose above $607 million\n- BTC accounted for about $190 million of the damage\n- Total crypto liquidations approached $677 million\n\n### Oil and Yields Added Pressure\n\nCrypto usually trades as a high-beta risk asset when macro stress rises. Once oil spiked above $103, markets had to price a more inflationary path and a firmer dollar.\n\nThat matters because higher yields reduce the appeal of leveraged growth and speculative bets. The same move that hurts equities can hit Bitcoin, especially after a sharp rally.\n\nGoogle News roundups of the selloff linked the drop to a wider risk-off move across majors and altcoins [across multiple reports](https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiugFBVV95cUxPdWljMVdkWmhveThjVVVqQkU2RngxQWhGUGVsaVNELUdzWGU2YU1OVmFpMktQd3h2RUdSOHg1dkRZeGdVQ0hyc0JHTWE5OVFSbGRreWRxQlAtZ3pZZTU3LTRIVzZVOVhEM1NhMVRxbVlscm9mV1FfYzUwMVBsRlR0ZDRhb1dOX0tQeDdCSEFFWmExLTJWMnI3ZThFZ2ROaGdUX2ZVYTc0VEpFMWVVLThTNjhmLTNlWi1uNGc?oc=5). That gave traders more reason to treat the slide as a broad de-risking event instead of a one-off Bitcoin move.\n\n## Key BTC support levels traders should watch now\n\nPrice is now sitting near the area that decides whether this becomes a short-lived shakeout or a deeper correction. The first test for buyers is simple: hold the recent flush above the mid-$76,000 range and stop liquidation-driven selling from extending.\n\n[CHART_PLACEHOLDER]\n\n### $76K Needs to Hold\n\nTraders were already focused on $76,000 as the first meaningful floor, and the market briefly tested that zone during the slide. If buyers defend it, Bitcoin can stabilize and rebuild above the high $70,000s. If it fails on volume, the market likely starts pricing a move toward the next demand pocket near $65,000, the downside area highlighted in the research set.\n\n### $80K Remains the Reclaim Level\n\nThe $80,000 to $83,000 band is now the overhead area bulls need to win back. A fast reclaim would suggest the Bitcoin selloff was mainly liquidation-driven, while repeated rejection would tell traders that macro pressure is still in control.\n\n- Look for: spot bids holding once liquidation volume fades\n- Look for: funding rates and open interest resetting without another hard leg lower\n- Look for: oil, yields, and dollar strength easing before BTC retests $80K\n\n## Conclusion\n\nThe Bitcoin selloff has pushed BTC back to the $76,000 area, with $677 million in crypto liquidations showing how quickly leverage unwound.\n\nNear-term structure now depends on whether buyers can defend support before macro headlines create another rush for the exit. Holding $76K keeps the move in pullback territory, but losing it would open a much deeper retracement.\n\nTraders should watch support, oil, and liquidation data together instead of treating this as a crypto-only event. If BTC cannot reclaim the high $70,000s quickly, stay defensive and let the market prove the bounce.\n\n## FAQs\n\n**1. Why did Bitcoin fall below $77K happen?**\nBitcoin fell below $77K after Trump warned that the \"clock is ticking\" for Iran, which triggered a broader risk-off move. Oil rose sharply, inflation worries returned, and traders cut exposure to leveraged assets. Crypto longs were already crowded after the recent rally. That mix turned a headline shock into forced selling.\n\n**2. Is this the start of a bigger correction?**\nPossibly, but the next step depends on $76K. If BTC holds that area and liquidation pressure cools, the move can still be treated as a reset inside a broader uptrend. If support breaks cleanly, traders will start pricing a trip toward deeper demand near $65K. The response after the first bounce matters more than the headline alone.\n\n**3. What levels and signals should traders watch now?**\nWatch $76K first and the $80K to $83K zone above it. Also track open interest, funding rates, and liquidation totals to see whether leverage has been fully cleared. Oil, Treasury yields, and dollar strength matter because they shape broader risk appetite. A calmer macro tape would improve the odds of stabilization.\n\n**4. How does this affect altcoins and the wider market?**\nThis kind of Bitcoin drop usually spills into high-beta names first. Ether, Solana, XRP, and smaller altcoins can underperform because traders pull risk from the edges of the market during stress. Crypto equities and ETF-linked sentiment can weaken as well. If BTC steadies, altcoins may recover, but they rarely lead during a geopolitical shock.\n\n**5. What is the historical context for this move?**\nBitcoin has a history of reacting like a risk asset during sudden macro or geopolitical scares. Similar episodes have produced fast liquidations, sharp weekend or overnight drops, and equally sharp relief bounces once forced selling ends. What makes this move stand out is the combination of a crowded long trade and oil above $103. That raises the macro sensitivity.\n\n**6. What are the short-term risks for investors?**\nThe main short-term risk is assuming the first dip is automatically a buying opportunity. If headlines worsen and $76K breaks, the market could search for liquidity much lower before finding real support. Another risk is overusing leverage in a headline-driven tape. Position size and patience matter more than conviction here.\n\n**Sources:**\n- CoinTelegraph: https://cointelegraph.com/markets/bitcoin-falls-to-76k-after-trump-says-clock-is-ticking-for-iran?utm_source=rss_feed&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound\n- CoinDesk: https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/05/18/bitcoin-slides-below-usd77-000-as-trump-s-iran-warning-rattles-risk-assets\n- Google News: https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiugFBVV95cUxPdWljMVdkWmhveThjVVVqQkU2RngxQWhGUGVsaVNELUdzWGU2YU1OVmFpMktQd3h2RUdSOHg1dkRZeGdVQ0hyc0JHTWE5OVFSbGRreWRxQlAtZ3pZZTU3LTRIVzZVOVhEM1NhMVRxbVlscm9mV1FfYzUwMVBsRlR0ZDRhb1dOX0tQeDdCSEFFWmExLTJWMnI3ZThFZ2ROaGdUX2ZVYTc0VEpFMWVVLThTNjhmLTNlWi1uNGc?oc=5\n\n[Word Count: XXXX]'''\nimport re\nprint('words', len(re.findall(r\"\\b\\S+\\b\", text)))\nprint('emdash', '—' in text)\nPY","workdir":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-writer","yieldMs":1000}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":1642,"output":5327,"cacheRead":8064,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":15033,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779109239761,"responseId":"chatcmpl-DgrsJi6zCsPOm4r77X9CWXBeH1dQw"}}
